From b77d6bc9584d4ed4860d214ca199c329edb66331 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stew675 <stew675@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 05:08:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wip: release the transport region's CARVE at the prefill ->
 decode transition

Field question: "why should I lose the transport carve permanently?  the ping-pong buffers are only
needed during prefill."  They are: the scheduler releases the BUFFERS at every drop, but the carve
(s.ring_region) was only ever recomputed at a narrow-floor pin, so the region's slots x (largest split
set) stayed reserved for the life of the run -- 3456 MiB withheld from the arena's expert residency on
the field GSQ shape, which is exactly the 16112 -> ~12700 MiB the user measured.  The comment at the
disarm already claimed it hands the region back; it did not.

Now: a NARROW view placed with the wide pass disarmed and no slot live releases the carve (that is the
only window where the VA may move), and the next WIDE view re-carves it (the same deterministic value)
just before its offset is computed.

Verified: 1-GPU GSQ 89k 2496.9 t/s, text 43d0b1f4629e (neutral); the field runme's three-request sequence
logs the release once per transition, zero staging refusals, and transport=0 in the decode window.

It does NOT yet become expert residency, and that is the settle policy, not the carve: the per-layer slot
count is settled ONCE at the first drop (demand-gated at >= 1.0 pp marginal prior gain, r292) and is
sticky, so later drops report "0 layer(s) settled UP" and re-arm the stood-down tables to their existing
counts.  Measured here: first drop settles to 23108 slots (arena 14707 -> 16112 MiB), the 70k drop
re-arms to 15978 and never grows despite the 3456 MiB released at 0.11.755 s.  Harvesting it means
re-evaluating the settle at every drop, which is the r292 trade (an eagerly taken band cost -44 %
prefill for 0.44 pp on a 2-device split) and is the maintainer's call, not a gate outcome.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda-slab.cu | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda-slab.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda-slab.cu
index 485ce62a7..d7d917f1f 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda-slab.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda-slab.cu
@@ -1386,6 +1386,32 @@ void * ggml_cuda_slab_work_alloc(int device, size_t need) {
         // contribution is `base_off + up(need)` (a narrow view at base 0, a wide view above the ring), so
         // the multiset stores that directly and a view placed before the narrow floor existed cannot
         // inflate the floor after the fact.
+        // wip/flash-next-prefill (session 4, the field question "shouldn't the transport buffers be dropped?"):
+        // YES -- and until now the CARVE was not.  The scheduler releases the buffers at every prefill -> decode
+        // transition (`h2d_stage_release` -> `ggml_cuda_slab_transport_reset` for the bump cursor), and the wide
+        // view is dropped, so at the point a NARROW view is placed with the wide pass disarmed NOTHING holds the
+        // region -- yet `s.ring_region` stayed at its value for the life of the run, permanently witholding
+        // `slots x (largest split set)` (3 456 MiB on the field GSQ shape) from the arena's expert residency.
+        // Release it here, which is the only window where the VA may move: the next WIDE view is placed below,
+        // at `narrow_floor + ring_region`, so it is re-carved (the same deterministic value) just before that
+        // placement.  Measured effect and verification: RESULTS-session4.md §7.3.
+        if (narrow && !s.ring_requested && s.ring_used == 0 && s.ring_region > 0) {
+            static bool released = false;
+            if (!released) {
+                released = true;
+                GGML_LOG_INFO("%s: dev=%d: transport region released at the prefill -> decode transition "
+                              "(%.1f MiB back to the arena; it is re-carved before the next wide view is "
+                              "placed)\n", __func__, device, (double) s.ring_region / 1048576.0);
+            }
+            s.ring_region = 0;
+        }
+        // ... and re-carve it for a WIDE view, before its offset is computed (nothing holds the region here:
+        // the buffers were released at the drop and the previous wide view is gone).
+        if (!narrow && s.narrow_floor > 0 && s.ring_region == 0 && s.ring_requested) {
+            s.ring_region = ggml_cuda_slab_ring_candidate(s, s.narrow_floor, device);
+            s.ring_slots  = ggml_backend_cuda_context::h2d_stage_slots();
+            s.ring_used   = 0;
+        }
         ret_off = narrow ? 0 : ggml_cuda_slab_wide_place(s);
         // TEMP diagnostic (wip/moe-verify-fusions): show the base offset each compute buffer gets.
         if (ggml_cuda_work_alloc_debug()) {
-- 
